 Deployment helpers for the internal services.
 
-`bin/notify-deploy.sh SERVICE VERSION` restarts the service on the deploy host and posts a
-message to the release channel. The webhook URL comes from `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` in the
-environment; per-service settings live in `etc/services.conf`.
+## notify-deploy.sh
+
+```
+bin/notify-deploy.sh [--dry-run] SERVICE VERSION [NOTE]
+```
+
+Restarts the service on the deploy host and posts a message to the release channel. The
+webhook URL comes from `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` in the environment; per-service settings live in
+`etc/services.conf`. Requires `jq`.
+
+- `SERVICE` must match `^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,63}$`.
+- `VERSION` must start with a letter or digit and contain only letters, digits, `.`, `_`, `+`
+  and `-` (up to 64 characters).
+- `NOTE` (optional) is a short release note, at most 300 characters with no control characters
+  (so a single line). Quote it so it is passed as one argument. It appears on its own line
+  under the "Deployed ..." message in Slack.
+- `--dry-run` validates the arguments, then prints the `ssh` command and the Slack message it
+  would send. It does not restart the service or post anything, and `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` is not
+  required (the URL is never printed).
+
+Examples:
+
+```
+bin/notify-deploy.sh web 1.4.2
+bin/notify-deploy.sh web 1.4.2 "Fixes login timeout on slow networks"
+bin/notify-deploy.sh --dry-run api 2.0.0 "Check the message before sending"
+```
+
+Exit statuses: 64 usage, 65 invalid argument, 69 missing `jq`, 78 missing or malformed
+`SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`.
